00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:47.148
OK, the government was way too calm
about everything leading up to this

00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:50.235
but if you think about it, their calm
reaction to the events

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:52.779
leading up to this actually makes sense. Why?

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:57.075
Japan is one of the few countries located above
what is called the Ring of Fire.

00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:58.743
Or the Circum Pacific Belt.

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:03.706
It's a path along the Pacific Ocean that traces
the boundaries between several tectonic plates.

00:02:03.706 --> 00:02:09.629
75% of the Earth's volcanoes,
more than 450 of them are located along this area.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:13.007
A large portion of the planet's
most violent acts happen here.

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:16.594
Japan is no slouch
when it comes to dealing with natural disasters.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:20.056
Since the archipelago is situated
along this ring of fire.

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:24.519
This country is vulnerable to natural disasters
such as earthquakes, tsunamis

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:26.562
and volcanic eruptions in fact.

00:02:26.562 --> 00:02:31.901
Japan is so used to all of this that it even has
a dedicated budget and massive systems in place

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.319
to deal with all of this.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.031
They've earthquake resistant buildings
that move with the earthquakes,

00:02:37.031 --> 00:02:39.617
which means that everything
these guys have experienced up to

00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:42.704
this point was pretty much
just another regular Tuesday,

00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:45.915
minus the giant, ugly
monster crushing its way through the city streets.

00:02:45.915 --> 00:02:47.625
And ruining people's lives.

00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:27.642
The creature going through tiny streets
